[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5383177355","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122708#issuecomment-5383177355","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122708","id":5383177355,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQNzEiw","user":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-22T23:36:24Z","updated_at":"2026-08-22T23:36:24Z","body":"Also reproducible on 4.6 and 4.8 dev 3.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5383177355/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6300068025","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122708#issuecomment-6300068025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122708","id":6300068025,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABd4NouQ","user":{"login":"shive1807","id":29089483,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MDg5NDgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29089483?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807","html_url":"https://github.com/shive1807","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-20T19:52:59Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T19:52:59Z","body":"Hi, thanks for the detailed report and the MRP, it made this easy to reproduce.\n\nI tested the MRP and was able to reproduce the issue. From what I can see, it seems related to the placement of the collision shapes: the player’s capsule can enter the narrow gap between the two capsules and the circle, but it can’t get back out once it’s there.\n\nIncreasing the CharacterBody2D’s safe_margin (to 2.0 in my test) gives the body enough clearance, and with that change I could no longer get the player stuck. I see you mentioned already trying safe_margin without reliable results, so it might depend on the specific value or the exact approach angle. It would be worth checking whether a similar value helps on your end.\n\nThis looks more like a workaround than a fix, since the body still shouldn’t be able to enter a position it can’t recover from. I’ll look further into the relevant physics code and update here if I find anything.\n\nTested on: Godot [v4.7.2.stable], [MacOS]\n\n<img width=\"419\" height=\"66\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6078b4f2-9285-4144-8372-141709cae27f\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6300068025/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6301302982","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122708#issuecomment-6301302982","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122708","id":6301302982,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABd5ZAxg","user":{"login":"shive1807","id":29089483,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MDg5NDgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29089483?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807","html_url":"https://github.com/shive1807","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shive1807/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-20T20:56:33Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T20:56:33Z","body":"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2a939319-3ca9-4372-80a6-18063aa0c459\n\nUpdate: After spending more time on this, I think I’ve found what’s happening.\n\nThe player’s capsule slides along the circle shape and ends up in a pocket formed by all three colliders (the two capsules and the circle). The capsule fits into that pocket almost exactly, so once it’s there, every direction it could move is blocked by at least one of the three shapes. There’s no path out.\n\nThis would also explain why increasing safe_margin helps: the extra clearance makes the body slightly larger for collision purposes, so it no longer fits into the pocket in the first place.\n\nSo this may be less a physics engine bug and more a geometry trap created by how the shapes are laid out. Still, it seems worth discussing whether the body should be able to slide into a position it can’t escape from. In practice, reasonable mitigations could be adjusting the collider placement or size so no pocket matches the player’s shape, or using a slightly larger safe_margin.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6301302982/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]